<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

</ix:nonNumeric><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="From2024-09-30to2025-09-28" escape="true" id="Fact000525" name="us-gaap:TradeAndOtherAccountsReceivablePolicy"><p id="xdx_84E_eus-gaap--TradeAndOtherAccountsReceivablePolicy_zUfsad2scGh5" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i><span id="xdx_86F_zyyQPXpWip4k">Accounts
Receivable</span>:</i></b> Optex Systems Holdings records its accounts receivable at the original sales invoice amount less liquidations for
previously collected advance/progress bills and an allowance for expected credit losses. As of the fiscal year beginning October 2, 2023,
the Company adopted Accounting Standards Update (ASU) 2016-13, &#8220;<i>Financial Instruments &#8211; Credit Losses (Topic 326): Measurement
of Credit Losses on Financial Instruments.&#8221;</i> Under the new standard, the current expected credit loss (&#8220;CECL&#8221;) model
is used for estimating an allowance for credit losses and an allowance is set up when the receivable is initially recorded, even if the
probability of loss is remote. The Company utilizes a CECL model based on the aging schedule method. As the customer base is primarily
U.S. government and government prime contractors, Optex Systems Holdings allowance for credit losses is minimal. On a quarterly basis,
Optex Systems Holdings evaluates its accounts receivable and establishes an allowance for credit losses, using a CECL model based on
a rolling aging schedule method. An account receivable is considered to be past due if any portion of the receivable balance is outstanding
beyond its scheduled due date. No interest is accrued on past due accounts receivable. As of September 28, 2025, and September 29, 2024,
Optex Systems Holdings had an allowance for credit losses of $<span id="xdx_908_eus-gaap--AllowanceForDoubtfulAccountsReceivable_iI_pn3n3_c20250928_z6HSyXnTkFm7" title="Allowance for doubtful accounts"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:AllowanceForDoubtfulAccountsReceivable" contextRef="AsOf2025-09-28" id="Fact000527" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-3" scale="3" unitRef="USD">5</ix:nonFraction> </span>thousand and $<span id="xdx_907_eus-gaap--AllowanceForDoubtfulAccountsReceivable_iI_pn3n3_c20240929_zT1hK2y3WcI7" title="Allowance for doubtful accounts"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:AllowanceForDoubtfulAccountsReceivable" contextRef="AsOf2024-09-29" id="Fact000529" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-3" scale="3" unitRef="USD">15</ix:nonFraction></span> thousand, respectively, for non U.S. government account
balances. Optex Systems Holdings charges uncollectible accounts to credit loss expense in the period in which they are first deemed uncollectible.
In the fiscal year 2025 we recognized $<span id="xdx_901_eus-gaap--ProvisionForDoubtfulAccounts_pn3n3_c20240930__20250928_zKhS66jaaSha" title="Bad debt expenses associated with uncollectible accounts"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ProvisionForDoubtfulAccounts" contextRef="From2024-09-30to2025-09-28" id="Fact000531" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-3" scale="3" unitRef="USD">4</ix:nonFraction></span> thousand in credit loss expenses associated with uncollectible accounts. In the fiscal year
2024 we recognized $<span id="xdx_90F_eus-gaap--ProvisionForDoubtfulAccounts_pn3n3_c20231002__20240929_zpSX7BMFazKi" title="Bad debt expenses associated with uncollectible accounts"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ProvisionForDoubtfulAccounts" contextRef="From2023-10-022024-09-29" id="Fact000533" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-3" scale="3" unitRef="USD">10</ix:nonFraction></span> thousand in credit loss expenses associated with uncollectible accounts.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">As
of September 28, 2025, <span id="xdx_90F_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20240930__20250928__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--EightCustomersMember_z8SK53mteKBa" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2024-09-302025-09-28_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_EightCustomersMember" id="Fact000535" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">91</ix:nonFraction></span>% of the accounts receivable balance was comprised of eight customers: the U.S. government, <span id="xdx_902_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20240930__20250928__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--USGovernmentAgenciesMember_zfNRBk8Hz2c8" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2024-09-302025-09-28_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_USGovernmentAgenciesMember" id="Fact000537" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">12</ix:nonFraction></span>%, seven major
defense contractors, <span id="xdx_900_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20240930__20250928__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorOneMember_zRGN0BxNq7E7" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2024-09-302025-09-28_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorOneMember" id="Fact000539" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">27</ix:nonFraction></span>%, <span id="xdx_90A_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20240930__20250928__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorTwoMember_zhETiCvjPjAj" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2024-09-302025-09-28_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorTwoMember" id="Fact000541" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">22</ix:nonFraction></span>%,<span id="xdx_903_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20240930__20250928__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorThreeMember_zsN9MvnzhW0g" title="Concentration risk percentage"> <ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2024-09-302025-09-28_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorThreeMember" id="Fact000543" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">8</ix:nonFraction></span>%, <span id="xdx_90A_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20240930__20250928__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorFourMember_zQPGiXu25xO3" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2024-09-302025-09-28_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorFourMember" id="Fact000545" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">6</ix:nonFraction></span>%, <span id="xdx_900_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20240930__20250928__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorFiveMember_zyfGrAir9ibh" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2024-09-302025-09-28_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorFiveMember" id="Fact000547" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">6</ix:nonFraction></span>%, <span id="xdx_902_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20240930__20250928__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorSixMember_zE9OCbefI1j4" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2024-09-302025-09-28_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorSixMember" id="Fact000549" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">5</ix:nonFraction></span>% and <span id="xdx_905_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20240930__20250928__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorSevenMember_z4RcO6xo0vPa" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2024-09-302025-09-28_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorSevenMember" id="Fact000551" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">5</ix:nonFraction></span>%. As of September 29, 2024, <span id="xdx_907_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20231002__20240929__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--SevenCustomersMember_zahcsMZPzbea" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2023-10-022024-09-29_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_SevenCustomersMember" id="Fact000553" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">79</ix:nonFraction></span>% of the accounts receivable balance was comprised
of seven customers: the U.S. government, <span id="xdx_906_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20231002__20240929__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--USGovernmentAgenciesMember_zJUhad6VjHg5" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2023-10-022024-09-29_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_USGovernmentAgenciesMember" id="Fact000555" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">15</ix:nonFraction></span>%, five major defense contractors, <span id="xdx_906_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20231002__20240929__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorOneMember_zUBRG1OQEbp4" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2023-10-022024-09-29_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorOneMember" id="Fact000557" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">26</ix:nonFraction></span>%, <span id="xdx_90E_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20231002__20240929__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorTwoMember_zWSvdF4mrgs" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2023-10-022024-09-29_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorTwoMember" id="Fact000559" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">10</ix:nonFraction></span>%, <span id="xdx_907_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20231002__20240929__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorThreeMember_zMZvS1jmtdzd" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2023-10-022024-09-29_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorThreeMember" id="Fact000561" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">9</ix:nonFraction></span>%, <span id="xdx_901_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20231002__20240929__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorFourMember_zr0FClp7cXbb" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2023-10-022024-09-29_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorFourMember" id="Fact000563" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">7</ix:nonFraction></span>% and <span id="xdx_904_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20231002__20240929__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--MajorUSDefenseContractorFiveMember_z5nbjQK7jS1i" title="Concentration risk percentage"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2023-10-022024-09-29_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_MajorUSDefenseContractorFiveMember" id="Fact000565" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">7</ix:nonFraction></span>%, and a foreign military customer,<span id="xdx_908_eus-gaap--ConcentrationRiskPercentage1_pid_dp_c20231002__20240929__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByBenchmarkAxis__us-gaap--AccountsReceivableMember__us-gaap--ConcentrationRiskByTypeAxis__us-gaap--CustomerConcentrationRiskMember__srt--MajorCustomersAxis__custom--ForeignMilitaryCustomerMember_zERJvukr2Wpc" title="Concentration risk percentage">
<ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ConcentrationRiskPercentage1" contextRef="From2023-10-022024-09-29_us-gaap_AccountsReceivableMember_us-gaap_CustomerConcentrationRiskMember_custom_ForeignMilitaryCustomerMember" id="Fact000567" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="INF" scale="-2" unitRef="Pure">5</ix:nonFraction></span>%.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

</ix:nonNumeric><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="From2024-09-30to2025-09-28" escape="true" id="Fact000569" name="us-gaap:InventoryPolicyTextBlock"><p id="xdx_848_eus-gaap--InventoryPolicyTextBlock_zBsiUIGlN5M7" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i><span id="xdx_860_z7WiDxo2OPf6">Inventory</span>:
</i></b>Inventory is recorded at the lower of cost or net realizable value and adjusted as appropriate for decreases in valuation and
obsolescence. Adjustments to the valuation and obsolescence reserves are made after analyzing market conditions, current and projected
sales activity, inventory costs and inventory balances to determine appropriate reserve levels. Cost is determined using the first-in
first-out method. As of September 28, 2025, and September 29, 2024 inventory included:</span></p>

<ix:nonNumeric contextRef="From2024-09-30to2025-09-28" escape="true" id="Fact000571" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfInventoryCurrentTableTextBlock"><p id="xdx_890_eus-gaap--ScheduleOfInventoryCurrentTableTextBlock_zWFpHnNLQ3vj" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span><span id="xdx_8B5_zRWJiT8EyJwl" style="display: none">Schedule of Inventory</span></p>

<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%">
